(Part: horn_adapter.step)
(Job: horn_adapter.job.json)
(Setup: top, tool axis +Z)
(WCS: G54 at stock_top_center)
(Z0: stock_top_center, on the top of the stock. After facing, the faced top is Z-1.000)
(Post: linuxcnc, for LinuxCNC, units mm, dwell P in seconds)
(T1: D6 mm flat_endmill 3 flutes 3FL carbide, aluminium: 10000 rpm, feed 1200 mm/min, plunge 360 mm/min)
(T2: D4 mm flat_endmill 2 flutes 2FL carbide, aluminium: 10000 rpm, feed 600 mm/min, plunge 180 mm/min)
(T3: D6 mm spot_drill: 4456 rpm, feed 534.7 mm/min)
(T4: D2.5 mm drill M3 tap drill: 10000 rpm, feed 622.5 mm/min)
(T5: D3.4 mm drill: 7864 rpm, feed 637 mm/min)
(T6: D3 mm tap M3x0.5 spiral point, floating holder: 600 rpm, feed 300 mm/min)
(T7: D6 mm chamfer_mill 90 deg carbide: 10000 rpm, feed 800 mm/min, plunge 240 mm/min)
(Tool length: every Z is the tool's lowest point, a drill's, spot drill's or chamfer mill's tip, a ball's bottom. Measure each tool's length there)
(Prove this program on the machine: single block, feed override low, in air first.)
